{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video was sponsored by Fasthosts,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2300,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who are offering UK viewers the chance to win a 5,000 pound tech bundle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6660,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you can answer my Techie Test question later in the show."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9960,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On May 1st, 2015 a group of scientists predicted that the following November,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15020,
    "dDurationMs": 8680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we would see a star go supernova billions of light years away in a spiral galaxy designated SP1149."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was the first time anyone had ever tried to predict a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29640,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for good reason: they are incredibly rare and unpredictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34660,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a star larger than 8 times the mass of our sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37600,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a supernova marks the end of its life cycle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Running out of fuel in its core, the star collapses in on itself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45040,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then, in the ensuing crush of matter, it violently explodes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50480,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A supernova can be as bright as a whole galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53600,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And importantly, the light emitted follows a predictable pattern:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it glows brightly for weeks and then fades down over a period of months"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63000,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But supernovae are rare."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64980,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In any galaxy of 100 billion stars or so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68480,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can expect on average only two per century."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72120,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So just try picking the star that is going to explode."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77260,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, we can say how long a given star will live based on its mass, luminosity and color temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82780,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These data pinpoint its stage of life in a predictable life cycle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86660,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the estimate of exactly when a large star will go supernova has big error bars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92220,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take the red supergiant Betelgeuse, for example, in our own Milky Way Galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96960,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a great candidate to go supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99580,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists think Betelgeuse will explode any day now in the next few..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103680,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundred thousand years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106020,
    "dDurationMs": 7540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it does, it'll be so bright you can see it in the daytime, and it will rival the full moon’s brightness at night."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114140,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Compared to the lifespan of a star, a hundred thousand years is a brief window of time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119860,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but for us short-lived humans, it may as well be forever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124260,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might think it would have been a tough sell when the scientists who predicted we’d see a supernova in November 2015"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129860,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asked for time on the Hubble Space Telescope to take pictures of galaxy SP1149."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135880,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But their request was granted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139100,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They could image this part of the sky roughly once a month starting on October 30th."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144400,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before this, the galaxy was too close to the sun to point Hubble at it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148920,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this first image taken at the end of October there is no supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154020,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next image was taken on Nov. 14"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157120,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, no Supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159940,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in third image, taken on Dec. 11th, jackpot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164000,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s a supernova right where they predicted it would be and almost exactly when they said it would happen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170520,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how did they manage to predict a supernova, almost to the month?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175060,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the truth is they had seen this same exact supernova before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180540,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not once, not twice, but four additional times!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185400,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A year earlier and five months before the predictions, Hubble took this image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189900,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See those 4 bright dots?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191700,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those are multiple images of that same supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194900,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reason we see the same supernova in four different locations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198220,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is because there is a lens between us and the exploding star"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202720,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not a lens made of glass of course but a gravitational lens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206540,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made of a huge amount of ordinary matter and dark matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211060,
    "dDurationMs": 7660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravitational lensing tends to magnify distant sources and increase their apparent brightness, as rays of light become concentrated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218720,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This smears the image of distant galaxies into arcs, strands, and all kinds of weird shapes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225120,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, to some distant observer in another galaxy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228620,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the light from our sun and Milky Way galaxy may be similarly warped"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233500,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In gravitational lensing, there are three essential components --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236840,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the source, the lens, and the telescope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240240,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the lens and the source are spherically symmetric,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243040,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if the source, lens, and telescope are all perfectly aligned,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247140,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get what’s known as an Einstein ring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251080,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The light from the source is bent around the lens, equally in all directions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255140,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leading to the image of a smeared out ring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259060,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the source and the lens are spherically symmetric, but are not perfectly aligned,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263460,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we end up seeing is a break in the Einstein ring --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266600,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it splits into two semi-circles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if the source, lens and telescope are aligned but the lens is not axially symmetric"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274720,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example it could have an elliptical shape -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277540,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you get four images in the shape of a cross, an Einstein cross."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283620,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happened to our supernova is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286440,
    "dDurationMs": 8100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "9.3 billion years ago, a dying star in a galaxy far, far away went out with a bang as a supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294540,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The explosion sent out a blast of light in all directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298280,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About 5 billion years ago, before the Earth even existed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301960,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that light encountered a very massive object that warped spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306780,
    "dDurationMs": 7800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was a cluster of galaxies called MACS J1149.5+2223."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314580,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(I know that’s a mouthful. But the name just tells us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317680,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where in the sky it was discovered by the MAssive Cluster Survey.)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322800,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This galaxy cluster is made of lots of massive substructures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326580,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like individual galaxies and halos of dark matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330140,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At some point as the light traveled through this region,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333260,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it encountered an elliptical galaxy almost perfectly lined up with where the Earth would eventually be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339920,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The gravitational deflection focused light rays that were initially diverging onto paths that converged at the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348140,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why we saw the same supernova in four different locations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353440,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only did the supernova appear at 4 different places,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356520,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the images also appeared at different times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360080,
    "dDurationMs": 6300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relative to the first image, the others were delayed by periods ranging from 5 days to over 3 weeks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366380,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We could measure this time delay because of the distinctive light-curve of the supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371540,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of the images of the explosion were further along in their light curve than others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376420,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was a particularly lucky discovery -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378880,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first time a multiply-lensed supernova has ever been observed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383160,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are other objects that due to gravitational lensing appear multiple times on the sky, like multiple images of galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390060,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But these objects don’t change predictably with time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392860,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so there is no way to use their images to work out the relative time delay between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398700,
    "dDurationMs": 6980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One reason for the time delay is because the four paths the light took were different lengths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405680,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it took the light longer to travel further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408780,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is another reason:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410980,
    "dDurationMs": 7720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light passing through curved spacetime appears to travel more slowly relative to an external observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418700,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is much less intuitive, but is a well established and well tested part of General Relativity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Back in 1964, Irwin Shapiro suggested"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427960,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would be possible to test this gravitational time delay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431260,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by sending radar signals to Venus, and measuring how long it takes for the echo to come back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436660,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He calculated that, due to the gravitational influence of the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440140,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the signals would take an extra 200 microseconds when Venus was on the other side of the sun compared to when it was close to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448600,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is solely a gravitational time delay, not related to the extra distance the light has to travel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454600,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And within a couple years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455960,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experimental data revealed the gravitational time delay for light traveling past the sun, was exactly as predicted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464140,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, in order to accurately determine the distance to the Voyager and Pioneer spacecraft,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469020,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this Shapiro time delay must be taken into account."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472800,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I want you to have a look at the four supernova images again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476440,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you notice how the same galaxy appears three times in this image?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481260,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the supernova’s host galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is itself lensed by the "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "massive galaxy cluster MACS J1149.5+2223"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492600,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, this cluster lenses tens of galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496480,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So scientists had been studying and modeling the distribution of matter in the cluster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501060,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long before the supernova."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502960,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They asked: if we see these four images of the supernova in one image of its host galaxy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508780,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when would the supernova appear in these other two images of the host galaxy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513560,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using the models of mass distribution and General Relativity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517160,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they calculated that in this image the supernova would have appeared twenty years earlier - in 1995!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525240,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now there are no close-up pictures of this part of the sky from 1995"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528780,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so there is no way to check."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531260,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the other image of the galaxy they predicted the supernova would appear again in about one year's time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538240,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Almost exactly when it showed up in that Hubble image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543000,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This successful prediction is a fantastic confirmation of our understanding of light and gravity on the scale of the whole universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550520,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it has even bigger implications."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553300,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the hottest debates in astronomy right now is:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556120,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how fast is our universe actually expanding?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559240,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is measured by the Hubble constant:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561620,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rate at which distant galaxies are receding, depending on their distance apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568040,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are two main ways this measurement has traditionally been made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571660,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One is to look for stars in the nearby universe whose absolute luminosity we know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577820,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then we can use how bright they appear to us to determine how far away they are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582560,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you combine this distance information with how redshifted their light is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586300,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can work out how fast the universe is expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589600,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as the distance ladder method"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592520,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the value of the Hubble constant it produces is around 74 kilometers per second per megaparsec."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598860,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meaning for every megaparsec that separates two galaxies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602560,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they will on average be moving apart at 74 km/s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607640,
    "dDurationMs": 6380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other way to measure the Hubble constant is to study the features in the cosmic microwave background radiation-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614020,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is essentially just a picture of the early universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617500,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using the standard model of cosmology (which is called Lambda-CDM)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621580,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can work out how this early universe picture would expand over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The result obtained from this method comes out to 67 kilometers per second per megaparsec,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631600,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "substantially slower than the 74 found via the other method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635700,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the years both of these techniques have been refined, reducing their uncertainties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640880,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the values have not gotten closer together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644260,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at this moment the two values really seem different -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648340,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are on the cusp of being a 5 sigma result."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652540,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Astrophysicist Joseph Silk has called it a “possible crisis for cosmology”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658040,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are independent ways to measure the Hubble constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of them is to look at a mutiply-lensed supernova"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664560,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and use the time delay between their appearances to work it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668800,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was first proposed by a Norwegian astronomer Sjur Refsdal in 1964."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674560,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since this is the first observed multiply-lensed supernova, it has become known as Supernova Refsdal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681040,
    "dDurationMs": 6580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Calculations of the Hubble constant from this data yield a value of 64 kilometers per second per megaparsec."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687620,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And although the result has large error bars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690200,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is more in line with the measurements of the cosmic microwave background than with the distance ladder method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696460,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The thing I keep thinking about is how strange space is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700620,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, I used to think of it essentially like glass, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703360,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fundamentally transparent with some foggy regions or some slight distortions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708120,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here we have space warping light on multiple curved trajectories,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712720,
    "dDurationMs": 9160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making the same event appear in six different places on the sky separated by days, weeks, a year and twenty years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722560,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what is contained in those distortions is information about the workings of our entire universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733580,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey this video was sponsored by Fasthosts,"
    } ]
